  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response Stranded Ethiopian Migrants in EHoA - Emergency response stranded migrants EHoA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Emergency Response Stranded Ethiopian Migrants in EHoA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IOM har ans&#xf6;kt om medel fr&#xe5;n Sida f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra projektet &#x201d;Facilitating safe return and reintegration of stranded vulnerable Ethiopian Migrants in the East and Horn of Africa&#x201d;. 

Projektperioden &#xe4;r 1 september 2021&#x2013;1 september 2022. Projektets &#xe4;ndam&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att bidra till en effektiv migrationshantering i &#xd6;stra Afrika och p&#xe5; Afrikas horn genom ett s&#xe4;kert &#xe5;terv&#xe4;ndande, st&#xf6;dinsatser vid &#xe5;terv&#xe4;ndande, och &#xe5;terintegrering av s&#xe4;rskilt utsatta etiopiska migranter.

IOM f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;r att st&#xf6;det skall anv&#xe4;ndas f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka organisationens kapacitet att bist&#xe5; s&#xe4;rskilt utsatta etiopiska migranter i &#xd6;stra Afrika och p&#xe5; Afrikas horn. Insatsen skall genomf&#xf6;ras under IOM:s ledning i Djibouti, Etiopien, Somalia, Tanzania och Jemen. 

Den totala budgeten f&#xf6;r insatsen uppg&#xe5;r till 20 000 000 kronor. Utbetalning av beloppet i sin helhet kommer g&#xf6;ras vid undertecknandet av avtalet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM) has applied to Sida for funds of SEK 20 000 000 to carry out the project&#x201d; Facilitating safe return and reintegration of stranded vulnerable Ethiopian Migrants in the East and Horn of Africa&#x201d;. The project will be conducted during a 12-month period, 1 September 2021- 1 September 2022.

The intervention aims to contribute to effective migration management in the East and Horn of Africa through safe and dignified return, post-arrival assistance and reintegration of vulnerable Ethiopian migrants. The interventions will cover Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia, the United Republic of Tanzania, and Yemen

The International Organization for Migration (IOM) will be the implementer of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to contribute to effective migration management in the East and Horn of Africa through safe and dignified return, post-arrival assistance and reintegration of vulnerable Ethiopian migrants. This is to be achieved through:

1. The provision of tailored humanitarian assistance and protection services in countries of origin and transit

2. Access to return, post-arrival and reintegration assistance in countries of origin and transit</narrative>
  </description>
